  "scopeNotes": [
    "Historic house Oudezijds Voorburgwal 40 and the two incorporated rear alley houses share BAG0363100012178021; entrance38 is separate BAG0363100012178040.",
    "Heintje Hoekssteeg remains open above ground; connection is underground and is deliberately not drawn as an opaque street bridge.",
    "Native WGS84 surveys inherited from cached canal-museum-footprints source. Heights 19.8/17.6 are envelope guidance, not uniform wall heights. Eaves14/14.8 and facade bay dimensions are photograph-derived approximations.",
    "Historic main facade four sash bays, white lower pui, basement and raised entry stairs, shoulder-scroll triangular gable with two lower attic windows and one upper; modern entrance three ungridded bays, recycled brick and red lintels, tile gable/dormer and rear roof lantern."
  ]
